  "awb---how-to-title": "How to Make a T Shirt Order Form",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"T Shirt Order Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a T-shirt order form used for?\", \"a\": \"A t shirt order form collects what each buyer wants printed: the style, color, size and quantity, along with their name and how they pay. Organizers use it to total every size for the printer before a print run.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a T-shirt order form online?\", \"a\": \"List the shirts and their prices, then decide when orders close. Describe that to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> and it builds a tshirt order form that takes payment and keeps a running count per size.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a T-shirt order form template for Word?\", \"a\": \"You can make one in Word in a few minutes with a table that gives each buyer a row and each size a column. Insert drop-down content controls from the Developer tab so the size column only accepts real sizes. Each returned copy still gets added up by hand.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to make a shirt order form on Google Forms?\", \"a\": \"Open a blank Google Form and add a dropdown for each choice the printer needs: style, color, and size. Add a short answer that accepts only numbers for the quantity, and one for the buyer's name. Responses land in a linked Google Sheet, where a pivot table totals each size. Google Forms takes no payment, though, so buyers pay through a separate link or in cash.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a printable T-shirt order form?\", \"a\": \"Template sites and print shops post free printable versions as PDF files. Pick a shirt order form template with a column for every size you print and room for back printing. Paper still leaves you collecting cash and typing totals into a spreadsheet.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a school T-shirt order form include?\", \"a\": \"Ask for the student's name and homeroom, a youth or adult size, and the quantity. Show the price and the date orders close. A good tshirt order form template for schools also names a contact for size swaps after delivery.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an editable T-shirt order form template?\", \"a\": \"Save the layout as a Word document, not a PDF or an image, and next year's prices and colors take a minute to change. An online form is editable too: change a price or add a color, and the next buyer sees it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a merchandise order form?\", \"a\": \"A merchandise order form covers more than shirts, such as hoodies, hats and tote bags, each with its own sizes or colors. Bands and clubs use one to take orders before printing. For goods that are not printed to order, a general order form fits better.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you fill in a T-shirt order form PDF?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A fillable PDF lets you click the size box and type straight into it. A flat one has no fields, but Acrobat Reader's Fill & Sign tool places typed text anywhere on the page, or you can print it and use a pen.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are T-shirt order forms free?\", \"a\": \"Printable t shirt order forms are free on many template sites. Building and publishing one in Emergent costs nothing on the free tier. When the shirt comes with a race entry, ask for the size on the registration form instead of a separate one.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---prompt": "<p>Build a t-shirt order form for my school that counts sizes for the printer.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a t-shirt order form for my school that counts sizes for the printer.\", \"chips\": [\"Build a t-shirt order form for my school where parents choose youth or adult sizes, and send the printer a total for each size when orders close.\", \"Make my t-shirt order form take card payments through my Stripe account, and add $3 to every 2XL or larger shirt.\", \"I need my school's t-shirt order form to close Friday at 3 pm, show a closed notice after that, and put late requests on a waitlist.\", \"Let each player on my team add a name on the back of their shirt for $5, and send the print shop a list of names grouped by size.\"]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
